{
  "uid": "home-slo",
  "title": "Service Availability",
  "description": "Is each public hostname actually answering, from outside the cluster? Probe-driven, so it covers the two services that bypass Traefik entirely and are invisible on every other dashboard.",
  "tags": ["selfhosted", "slo"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": { "from": "now-24h", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "cluster",
        "type": "constant",
        "query": "home-k3s",
        "current": { "text": "home-k3s", "value": "home-k3s" },
        "hide": 2
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Reachability — from a prober inside the cluster, out through the public path",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Currently up",
      "gridPos": { "h": 5, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
          "expr": "probe_success{cluster=\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            { "type": "value", "options": { "0": { "text": "DOWN", "color": "red", "index": 0 }, "1": { "text": "up", "color": "green", "index": 1 } } }
          ],
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "green", "value": 1 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }, "colorMode": "background", "textMode": "value_and_name", "orientation": "horizontal" }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Uptime over the selected range",
      "description": "The fraction of probes that succeeded. Probes run every 2 minutes, so a single 5-minute blip is visible but small.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 11, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
          "expr": "sort(100 * avg_over_time(probe_success{cluster=\"$cluster\"}[$__range]))",
          "instant": true,
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        { "id": "organize", "options": { "excludeByName": { "Time": true, "__name__": true, "cluster": true, "job": true }, "renameByName": { "Value": "uptime %", "instance": "service" } } },
        { "id": "sortBy", "options": { "sort": [{ "field": "uptime %", "desc": false }] } }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "percent", "decimals": 2 },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "uptime %" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "custom.cellOptions", "value": { "type": "color-background", "mode": "gradient" } },
              { "id": "thresholds", "value": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 95 }, { "color": "green", "value": 99.5 }] } }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "showHeader": true }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Probe response time",
      "gridPos": { "h": 11, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 6 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
          "expr": "probe_duration_seconds{cluster=\"$cluster\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 0, "lineWidth": 1 } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "calcs": ["mean", "max"] }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "TLS",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Certificate expiry — as seen from outside",
      "description": "What the public actually gets. For diemer.codes hostnames this is Cloudflare's edge certificate, not the cluster's; jellyfin.diemer.codes is the VPS Caddy's own Let's Encrypt cert.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 18 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
          "expr": "sort((probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry{cluster=\"$cluster\"} - time()) / 86400)",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "d", "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 14 }, { "color": "green", "value": 30 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "displayMode": "gradient", "orientation": "horizontal", "showUnfilled": true, "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] } }
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Traefik's own certificates",
      "description": "The cluster-side wildcard from the DuckDNS ACME DNS-01 resolver. Distinct from the panel on the left: this is the cert Traefik serves, which for Cloudflare-fronted hostnames the public never sees.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 18 },
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "__PROM_UID__" },
          "expr": "sort((traefik_tls_certs_not_after{cluster=\"$cluster\"} - time()) / 86400)",
          "instant": true,
          "legendFormat": "{{cn}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "d", "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 14 }, { "color": "green", "value": 30 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": { "displayMode": "gradient", "orientation": "horizontal", "showUnfilled": true, "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] } }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Serving quality — for the services behind Traefik",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 27 },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Success rate by hostname",
      "description": "Reachability and correctness are different questions. A probe can succeed against a hostname that is returning 500s to every real user — this panel is the second question, from the access log.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 28 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "__LOKI_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "__LOKI_UID__" },
          "expr": "sort(100 * sum by (RequestHost) (count_over_time({cluster=\"$cluster\", app=\"traefik\", DownstreamStatus!~\"5..\"}[$__range])) / sum by (RequestHost) (count_over_time({cluster=\"$cluster\", app=\"traefik\"}[$__range])))",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        { "id": "organize", "options": { "excludeByName": { "Time": true }, "renameByName": { "Value": "non-5xx %" } } },
        { "id": "sortBy", "options": { "sort": [{ "field": "non-5xx %", "desc": false }] } }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": { "unit": "percent", "decimals": 2 },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "non-5xx %" },
            "properties": [
              { "id": "custom.cellOptions", "value": { "type": "color-background", "mode": "gradient" } },
              { "id": "thresholds", "value": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 99 }, { "color": "green", "value": 99.9 }] } }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": { "showHeader": true }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "5xx rate by hostname",
      "description": "[may-be-empty] Flat zero is the expected state.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 28 },
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "__LOKI_UID__" },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "__LOKI_UID__" },
          "expr": "sum by (RequestHost) (rate({cluster=\"$cluster\", app=\"traefik\", DownstreamStatus=~\"5..\"}[5m]))",
          "queryType": "range",
          "legendFormat": "{{RequestHost}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "reqps", "custom": { "fillOpacity": 25, "lineWidth": 1, "drawStyle": "bars", "stacking": { "mode": "normal" } } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom" }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" } }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Coverage",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 38 },
      "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What these probes do and do not prove",
      "gridPos": { "h": 9, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 39 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**What is probed.** The sixteen public hostnames on the Cloudflare Tunnel, plus the two paths that bypass Traefik entirely — `jellyfin.diemer.codes` (VPS Caddy → NodePort `:30096`) and a TCP connect to `minecraft.diemer.codes:25565` (VPS haproxy). Those last two have no access log anywhere; a probe is the *only* signal they exist.\n\n**`*.zachd.duckdns.org` is deliberately not probed.** Since `infra/duckdns` moved to `updater.mode: tailnet`, those names resolve to a Tailscale `100.x` address that cluster pods cannot reach. A probe would report a permanent, meaningless outage.\n\n**A successful probe means \"the edge answered\", not \"the service works.\"** The `http_edge` module accepts 2xx, 3xx, 401 and 403, because most of these hostnames sit behind Authelia forward-auth and correctly answer an unauthenticated probe with a 302 to the portal. Application correctness is the *Serving quality* row above, and the 5xx panels on **Edge Traffic**.\n\n**The prober shares the cluster's fate.** It runs as a one-replica Deployment in the `alloy` namespace (`infra/alloy/values-probe.yaml`). If the cluster is down, the prober is down too, and these panels go to *No data* rather than to *DOWN*. **Treat a gap here as an outage, not as silence.** A genuinely external checker — Grafana Cloud Synthetic Monitoring, or anything hosted off-cluster — is the fix, and is not set up yet.\n\n**Why a prober at all, when Traefik metrics exist?** Traefik can only report on requests that arrived. If DNS breaks, the tunnel drops, or a certificate expires, the access log goes quiet — which is indistinguishable from a quiet night. The probe asks the question rather than waiting for someone else to."
      }
    }
  ]
}
